1
00:00:05,034 --> 00:00:07,264
Yomogi Kindergarten

2
00:00:12,744 --> 00:00:13,864
There.

3
00:00:16,014 --> 00:00:18,984
Oh... That one's damaged too, is it?

4
00:00:20,284 --> 00:00:22,514
I hope we could purchase new ones.

5
00:00:24,324 --> 00:00:26,484
If we fix them, they can still be used.

6
00:00:26,724 --> 00:00:29,194
Besides, new isn't everything.

7
00:00:31,164 --> 00:00:32,924
How are your university studies going?

8
00:00:33,364 --> 00:00:35,354
How? Ah, the same as always.

9
00:00:35,534 --> 00:00:36,894
Are you going to classes?

10
00:00:37,064 --> 00:00:38,434
Are you getting your credits?

11
00:00:39,234 --> 00:00:40,534
Of course.

12
00:00:40,534 --> 00:00:41,794
That's good.

13
00:00:42,874 --> 00:00:46,234
I was concerned because
you're always working.

14
00:00:48,714 --> 00:00:50,284
Good morning, Kobato!

15
00:00:50,284 --> 00:00:51,744
Good Mor...

16
00:00:52,584 --> 00:00:54,454
There she goes again! Kobato fell!

17
00:00:54,454 --> 00:00:56,184
You're all covered in dirt!

18
00:00:56,184 --> 00:00:57,454
Are you all right, Kobato?

19
00:00:57,454 --> 00:00:58,424
Give me a break.
Are you all right, Kobato?

20
00:00:58,424 --> 00:01:01,414
Who trips where there's nothing to trip over?

21
00:01:04,664 --> 00:01:06,324
Ow...

22
00:01:07,694 --> 00:01:10,064
Oh uh, thank you.

23
00:01:20,614 --> 00:01:23,744
Kobato.

24
00:01:23,744 --> 00:01:26,584
Kobato.
What should I do?

25
00:01:26,584 --> 00:01:30,984
Kobato.
Even the most obvious of things

26
00:01:31,884 --> 00:01:35,194
Are always such a challenge

27
00:01:35,194 --> 00:01:37,964
I want to laugh when I'm happy

28
00:01:37,964 --> 00:01:42,264
And sing whenever I want

29
00:01:42,834 --> 00:01:45,264
Is all

30
00:01:46,564 --> 00:01:50,934
They say my dreams will come true someday

31
00:01:51,374 --> 00:01:54,644
But when will "someday" come?

32
00:01:54,644 --> 00:01:58,134
I can't wait forever

33
00:01:58,284 --> 00:02:04,054
On "1, 2, 3!" I'll spread open my arms

34
00:02:04,054 --> 00:02:09,254
And let the light gather around me

35
00:02:09,254 --> 00:02:12,094
Where is it?

36
00:02:12,094 --> 00:02:15,434
Please tell me what I can do

37
00:02:15,434 --> 00:02:18,264
I make the most of getting hurt

38
00:02:18,264 --> 00:02:21,174
And run with all my might

39
00:02:21,174 --> 00:02:25,144
Despite how many dozens of times I fall

40
00:02:25,144 --> 00:02:28,174
And start crying

41
00:02:28,174 --> 00:02:32,204
I surprise myself

42
00:02:32,684 --> 00:02:36,844
In how much I believe in tomorrow

43
00:02:46,724 --> 00:02:48,994
...Gentle Person.

44
00:02:48,994 --> 00:02:50,024
...Gentle Person.
Fujimoto.

45
00:02:51,964 --> 00:02:55,064
Let me help you. Please. I'd like to!

46
00:02:56,034 --> 00:02:57,164
Whatever.

47
00:02:58,404 --> 00:02:59,374
Yes!

48
00:03:05,814 --> 00:03:07,804
Um... Fujimoto?

49
00:03:09,284 --> 00:03:12,084
There's something I've been wanting to ask you!

50
00:03:14,554 --> 00:03:15,794
Fujimoto?

51
00:03:15,794 --> 00:03:17,584
Be quiet and move your hands.

52
00:03:17,824 --> 00:03:19,854
Seeing that you have plenty
of time to open your mouth.

53
00:03:20,434 --> 00:03:21,624
Okay.

54
00:03:24,634 --> 00:03:25,464
What is it?

55
00:03:25,464 --> 00:03:26,594
Yes?

56
00:03:26,664 --> 00:03:29,004
What is it you've been wanting to ask me?

57
00:03:29,004 --> 00:03:30,634
Oh? Ah, yes...

58
00:03:31,174 --> 00:03:32,164
Well...

59
00:03:33,074 --> 00:03:36,304
It's about that strange phone call the other day.

60
00:03:38,284 --> 00:03:41,044
Why am I not to tell Ms. Sayaka about it?

61
00:03:42,914 --> 00:03:44,354
Just because.

62
00:03:44,784 --> 00:03:47,154
Why "just because"?

63
00:03:48,424 --> 00:03:51,394
If you can't keep it a secret, stop coming here.

64
00:03:54,564 --> 00:03:58,124
If you tell her, you'll upset her. That's why.

65
00:03:58,564 --> 00:04:01,664
Upset? Ms. Sayaka?

66
00:04:17,124 --> 00:04:20,144
Do you want to help? Or do you
just want to get in my way?

67
00:04:27,064 --> 00:04:28,994
What's the matter, Kobato?

68
00:04:30,364 --> 00:04:33,634
Fujimoto's mad at me again.

69
00:04:33,704 --> 00:04:35,074
Did he scold you?

70
00:04:35,074 --> 00:04:39,904
Yes. Because I keep getting in his
way when he's trying to work.

71
00:04:41,514 --> 00:04:44,114
I think you should apologize, then.

72
00:04:44,114 --> 00:04:46,174
We'll go and apologize with you.

73
00:04:47,954 --> 00:04:49,544
No!
They have just been painted so do not touch!

74
00:05:02,234 --> 00:05:05,924
I think he gets angry because
he worries about you.

75
00:05:06,504 --> 00:05:07,934
Do you think so?

76
00:05:07,934 --> 00:05:10,664
Of course, Kobato. Lighten up.

77
00:05:10,804 --> 00:05:14,604
My mom tells me she scolds me because
she expects me to be a good kid.

78
00:05:14,874 --> 00:05:20,474
You're right. I'll apologize and
ask him to let me help again.

79
00:05:22,884 --> 00:05:23,824
Huh?

80
00:05:23,824 --> 00:05:24,984
He's not here.

81
00:05:30,564 --> 00:05:32,284
I wonder what this is.

82
00:05:33,424 --> 00:05:36,764
Huh? That's probably Fujimoto's essay.

83
00:05:37,104 --> 00:05:38,494
Essay?

84
00:05:39,134 --> 00:05:40,794
I think he's going to need this today.

85
00:05:41,204 --> 00:05:43,574
Kobato, would you please take this to him?

86
00:05:43,774 --> 00:05:45,504
You want me to go?

87
00:05:45,774 --> 00:05:47,934
He'd probably be in trouble without it.

88
00:05:48,074 --> 00:05:50,044
Then I will take it to him!

89
00:05:55,384 --> 00:05:58,014
What's up? You're awfully upbeat.

90
00:05:58,384 --> 00:06:00,854
I need to have him acknowledge that
I don't always get in the way.

91
00:06:00,854 --> 00:06:03,724
That I can be helpful at times.

92
00:06:05,864 --> 00:06:10,734
The place called "university" that
Fujimoto goes to is this way, isn't it?

93
00:06:11,064 --> 00:06:13,464
I hope you got directions on how to get there!

94
00:06:13,634 --> 00:06:17,264
Yes. But what is "university"?

95
00:06:18,144 --> 00:06:20,404
You mean you came all this way
without even knowing that?!

96
00:06:21,014 --> 00:06:25,004
Not that your ignorance surprises me anymore.

97
00:06:25,784 --> 00:06:29,654
A university is a place where
people study difficult things.

98
00:06:29,754 --> 00:06:31,224
They study?

99
00:06:31,224 --> 00:06:35,454
Yeah. Like you know, if there's something you
want to do, or a career you want to pursue.

100
00:06:35,894 --> 00:06:37,514
Something you want to do...

101
00:06:42,164 --> 00:06:45,494
All these people. Look at all the people!

102
00:06:45,904 --> 00:06:47,134
Well it is a university after all.

103
00:06:47,534 --> 00:06:48,764
It's to be expected.

104
00:06:49,774 --> 00:06:52,544
How many Yomogi Kindergartens
could fit in here, do you think?

105
00:06:52,544 --> 00:06:54,004
Why are you comparing?!

106
00:06:57,144 --> 00:06:58,634
Just hurry up and find him!

107
00:06:58,984 --> 00:07:00,574
Yes sir, Ioryogi-san!

108
00:07:03,514 --> 00:07:04,544
Um...

109
00:07:08,494 --> 00:07:09,424
Um...

110
00:07:13,494 --> 00:07:15,794
U-Um, sorry!

111
00:07:18,164 --> 00:07:20,894
Um... well... huh?

112
00:07:21,174 --> 00:07:22,864
Stop getting lost!

113
00:07:25,644 --> 00:07:28,344
He's nowhere around. Fujimoto.

114
00:07:28,344 --> 00:07:31,904
But all we're doing is
roaming around the campus!

115
00:07:34,914 --> 00:07:36,714
Kobato is ready!

116
00:07:38,824 --> 00:07:40,344
It's Fujimoto!

117
00:07:45,994 --> 00:07:47,554
What are you waiting for?

118
00:07:50,094 --> 00:07:52,894
Yes of course, I have to get this to him!

119
00:07:55,274 --> 00:07:57,364
Hey, hey! Don't trip again!

120
00:08:03,074 --> 00:08:04,774
Sorry. Are you all right?

121
00:08:05,544 --> 00:08:06,744
Yes.

122
00:08:06,744 --> 00:08:07,774
Oh!

123
00:08:08,214 --> 00:08:09,844
No, it was my fault. Sorry.

124
00:08:09,914 --> 00:08:11,814
No worries, I'm okay.

125
00:08:12,484 --> 00:08:14,854
That's a cute little doll you have. Here you go.

126
00:08:15,454 --> 00:08:16,984
Thank you very much.

127
00:08:17,424 --> 00:08:20,794
Oh, and this... Are you a friend of Fujimoto?

128
00:08:20,794 --> 00:08:21,634
No!

129
00:08:21,634 --> 00:08:25,654
Well, I mean, I'm not his friend, but um...

130
00:08:26,264 --> 00:08:27,364
Kind of like a friend?

131
00:08:27,534 --> 00:08:29,664
Ah, yes. Maybe.

132
00:08:30,744 --> 00:08:31,674
Me too.

133
00:08:31,674 --> 00:08:33,334
Huh? And you are?

134
00:08:33,544 --> 00:08:37,214
Oh. I'm Takashi Domoto. And you?

135
00:08:37,214 --> 00:08:39,874
H-How do you do?! I'm Kobato Hanato!

136
00:08:40,344 --> 00:08:43,614
I came here to deliver Fujimoto
something he forgot.

137
00:08:43,614 --> 00:08:45,414
Fujimoto!

138
00:08:47,724 --> 00:08:50,154
I was sure he was around here somewhere.

139
00:08:50,764 --> 00:08:52,394
He ran off.

140
00:08:52,394 --> 00:08:53,324
What?

141
00:08:53,494 --> 00:08:56,734
Actually, I said something that upset him.

142
00:08:56,734 --> 00:08:58,394
Again?

143
00:08:58,504 --> 00:08:59,504
"Again"?

144
00:08:59,504 --> 00:09:01,974
Fujimoto always gets mad!

145
00:09:01,974 --> 00:09:03,304
Oh, but, but!

146
00:09:03,304 --> 00:09:07,534
That's because I'm always messing up.

147
00:09:07,874 --> 00:09:10,434
But still! I think he gets mad too often!

148
00:09:10,584 --> 00:09:16,514
Oh, but no... I'm always the one at
fault. He's done nothing wrong.

149
00:09:21,424 --> 00:09:22,594
I see.

150
00:09:22,594 --> 00:09:23,864
So you're from Yomogi Kindergarten.

151
00:09:23,864 --> 00:09:26,794
Yes! I help there!

152
00:09:27,294 --> 00:09:30,854
Gotcha! Why don't we look for
Fujimoto together, Kobato.

153
00:09:31,004 --> 00:09:33,794
You sure? Are you sure you don't mind?

154
00:09:34,134 --> 00:09:35,704
Would I be getting in your way?

155
00:09:35,704 --> 00:09:38,734
Oh no, of course not! I'd appreciate that!

156
00:09:39,274 --> 00:09:40,504
Great!

157
00:09:58,964 --> 00:10:02,624
Right now... he's probably in Philosophy of Law.

158
00:10:03,464 --> 00:10:06,764
Don't worry, I'm sure he's
at school all day today.

159
00:10:08,074 --> 00:10:10,204
I don't think he can afford
the time to work much.

160
00:10:10,204 --> 00:10:11,574
Is that right?

161
00:10:12,174 --> 00:10:13,644
It's almost exam time.

162
00:10:13,944 --> 00:10:17,844
Fujimoto always looks busy.

163
00:10:18,214 --> 00:10:19,574
You're right.

164
00:10:20,554 --> 00:10:23,144
In his case, he'd have an easy time
with any seminar he wanted,

165
00:10:23,414 --> 00:10:25,284
but he chooses to make work his priority.

166
00:10:26,024 --> 00:10:29,184
Well, that's what makes him Fujimoto.

167
00:10:29,854 --> 00:10:31,124
Hey Domoto!

168
00:10:31,824 --> 00:10:32,964
Do me a favor!

169
00:10:32,964 --> 00:10:33,894
What is it?

170
00:10:33,894 --> 00:10:35,424
We need your help!

171
00:10:35,494 --> 00:10:39,734
It's the paper for Professor Hayakawa.
We don't know where to begin!

172
00:10:39,734 --> 00:10:42,334
How can he expect us to
have it in by next week?

173
00:10:42,334 --> 00:10:44,704
All right, all right. I'll help you.

174
00:10:44,704 --> 00:10:45,574
Yay!

175
00:10:45,574 --> 00:10:47,404
Thanks, Domoto.

176
00:10:47,614 --> 00:10:51,234
You do understand that I'm just going to
help you. You've got to do the work.

177
00:10:51,644 --> 00:10:53,044
We know!

178
00:10:53,244 --> 00:10:54,374
Anyway, thanks!

179
00:10:55,054 --> 00:10:56,314
Oh, well.

180
00:10:57,624 --> 00:10:58,844
Let's go.

181
00:10:59,984 --> 00:11:02,284
Fujimoto? Haven't seen him.

182
00:11:02,924 --> 00:11:04,354
Did you try the library?

183
00:11:04,924 --> 00:11:06,124
Thanks.

184
00:11:06,124 --> 00:11:10,294
If you see him, could you let him
know I'm looking for him?

185
00:11:10,294 --> 00:11:10,834
What?!

186
00:11:10,834 --> 00:11:11,364
No way!
What?!

187
00:11:11,364 --> 00:11:12,064
No way!

188
00:11:12,304 --> 00:11:15,374
The guy's unfriendly. He intimidates me.

189
00:11:15,374 --> 00:11:16,834
He's not like that.

190
00:11:16,904 --> 00:11:18,644
No, really, I can't. Sorry.

191
00:11:18,644 --> 00:11:19,904
H-Hey...

192
00:11:22,444 --> 00:11:26,414
Is everyone afraid of Fujimoto?

193
00:11:26,414 --> 00:11:27,314
Huh?

194
00:11:27,314 --> 00:11:32,814
Well, you know. He isn't the outgoing type. And
he always looks like he's angry at something.

195
00:11:33,124 --> 00:11:34,484
To you, too?

196
00:11:35,254 --> 00:11:38,554
Well you said that you'd made him angry.

197
00:11:39,794 --> 00:11:43,024
Fujimoto had reason to get mad.

198
00:11:43,964 --> 00:11:47,664
He's always been the type not
to need help from anybody.

199
00:11:48,774 --> 00:11:53,474
But I opened my big mouth and kind of
gave him advice about his future.

200
00:11:54,444 --> 00:11:58,604
I've been aware of his personality for a very long
time. I should've just kept my mouth shut.

201
00:11:59,014 --> 00:12:00,274
Why is that?

202
00:12:04,354 --> 00:12:06,944
Well, I just can't turn my back on the guy.

203
00:12:09,024 --> 00:12:10,724
Ms. Sayaka!

204
00:12:11,064 --> 00:12:12,124
What is it?

205
00:12:12,124 --> 00:12:13,684
We're all waiting for you!

206
00:12:13,864 --> 00:12:15,694
Come on, let's play!

207
00:12:15,934 --> 00:12:22,134
Oh I'm sorry. You're bored because
Fujimoto and Kobato aren't here today.

208
00:12:23,034 --> 00:12:24,564
N-No, it's not that!

209
00:12:26,444 --> 00:12:28,174
Wait just a little bit longer, okay?

210
00:12:28,314 --> 00:12:29,744
Ms. Sayaka!

211
00:12:30,814 --> 00:12:32,214
Someone's here to see you!

212
00:12:33,844 --> 00:12:35,744
Hello!

213
00:12:36,084 --> 00:12:38,454
It's Chiho and Chise!

214
00:12:39,454 --> 00:12:40,644
Chitose?

215
00:12:41,024 --> 00:12:42,224
What's the matter?

216
00:12:42,224 --> 00:12:43,214
Guess what?

217
00:12:43,594 --> 00:12:46,114
Mommy and Chiho and I
made some macaroons!

218
00:12:46,294 --> 00:12:48,664
So we brought them for you to try!

219
00:12:49,294 --> 00:12:50,364
Right?

220
00:12:50,364 --> 00:12:51,624
Oh my...

221
00:12:51,764 --> 00:12:54,064
Thank you!

222
00:12:54,204 --> 00:12:55,434
These are good!

223
00:12:55,434 --> 00:12:56,924
Light and crispy!

224
00:12:58,144 --> 00:12:59,104
Sayaka.

225
00:12:59,444 --> 00:13:01,174
Where are Fujimoto and Kobato?

226
00:13:01,674 --> 00:13:04,474
They're at the university today.

227
00:13:05,384 --> 00:13:06,674
Kobato too?

228
00:13:07,984 --> 00:13:10,474
Fujimoto? I just saw him leave.

229
00:13:10,954 --> 00:13:14,714
I see. Thanks. We'll look elsewhere then.

230
00:13:15,094 --> 00:13:16,254
Hey Domoto!

231
00:13:17,624 --> 00:13:20,094
You get along well with
Professor Tomita, don't you?

232
00:13:20,594 --> 00:13:22,864
Could you put in a word for me?

233
00:13:23,264 --> 00:13:24,564
I can't afford to drop this credit.

234
00:13:24,964 --> 00:13:26,404
Have you told him yourself?

235
00:13:26,504 --> 00:13:28,834
Naw, it's kind of awkward you know?

236
00:13:28,834 --> 00:13:30,904
He values your opinion.

237
00:13:30,904 --> 00:13:32,534
If you could just break the ice with one word...

238
00:13:33,344 --> 00:13:35,314
All right, I'll mention you.

239
00:13:35,474 --> 00:13:37,634
For real?! Thanks, I owe you one!

240
00:13:38,044 --> 00:13:39,444
But you've got to go and talk
to him yourself afterwards.

241
00:13:39,444 --> 00:13:39,914
I know that. Thanks, I appreciate it!

242
00:13:39,914 --> 00:13:42,584
Everyone relies on Domoto
don't they, Ioryogi-san?
I know that. Thanks, I appreciate it!

243
00:13:42,584 --> 00:13:44,174
Everyone relies on Domoto
don't they, Ioryogi-san?

244
00:13:46,384 --> 00:13:47,484
Kobato.

245
00:13:47,794 --> 00:13:48,824
Sorry to keep you waiting.

246
00:13:48,824 --> 00:13:50,654
Not at all.

247
00:13:51,464 --> 00:13:53,054
Do you mind if we stop by somewhere?

248
00:13:53,324 --> 00:13:54,664
Oh, okay...

249
00:13:57,534 --> 00:14:01,364
I know you mean well, but he's
missed too many classes.

250
00:14:02,004 --> 00:14:04,134
And he feels very bad about it.

251
00:14:04,444 --> 00:14:07,504
Please, Professor. Could you
possibly overlook that part?

252
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:12,034
I understand. If you really insist.

253
00:14:12,184 --> 00:14:13,514
Thank you, sir.

254
00:14:17,754 --> 00:14:18,944
Sorry to keep you.

255
00:14:19,054 --> 00:14:20,954
Domoto, you're amazing.

256
00:14:20,954 --> 00:14:23,084
Amazing? Why?

257
00:14:23,694 --> 00:14:28,064
So many people rely on you
and you help everybody out.

258
00:14:28,494 --> 00:14:29,754
You think so?

259
00:14:29,894 --> 00:14:31,364
Yes!

260
00:14:31,364 --> 00:14:39,204
I really want to help others out, but I can't
do that well. I respect you, Domoto.

261
00:14:40,374 --> 00:14:43,834
Thank you... I guess...

262
00:14:43,944 --> 00:14:45,144
Huh?

263
00:14:46,084 --> 00:14:49,014
Oh, no, nothing. Shall we go?

264
00:14:49,014 --> 00:14:50,504
Ah, yes!

265
00:14:51,384 --> 00:14:53,184
One, two, three!

266
00:14:53,724 --> 00:14:55,714
Oh no, I lost!

267
00:14:56,224 --> 00:15:00,184
Well then Chiho, you're it. Everyone, let's hide!

268
00:15:03,364 --> 00:15:06,024
One! Two!

269
00:15:07,104 --> 00:15:10,094
I see. So she went to the university.

270
00:15:10,304 --> 00:15:13,134
She was quite excited about taking it to him.

271
00:15:13,244 --> 00:15:15,004
That sounds like Kobato.

272
00:15:16,414 --> 00:15:19,384
Oh. Sayaka, I want you to look at these.

273
00:15:21,814 --> 00:15:22,904
Yukari?

274
00:15:24,424 --> 00:15:25,474
Chise?

275
00:15:27,324 --> 00:15:29,124
Wh-Which are you?

276
00:15:31,464 --> 00:15:33,794
Gotcha, Yukari!

277
00:15:33,794 --> 00:15:35,924
Ch-Chiho, it was you?!

278
00:15:36,894 --> 00:15:41,394
This person says he might be
able to help you with a loan.

279
00:15:42,174 --> 00:15:44,574
This is an accountant friend of mine.

280
00:15:44,844 --> 00:15:46,564
And this person...

281
00:15:46,804 --> 00:15:48,534
I'm sorry Chitose.

282
00:15:49,844 --> 00:15:51,814
Sayaka, do you understand?

283
00:15:53,114 --> 00:15:56,884
I'm not trying to help you
because I feel sorry for you.

284
00:15:56,884 --> 00:16:03,124
It's because I want to protect the kindergarten
that my children and I all graduated from.

285
00:16:04,024 --> 00:16:06,894
So no more apologizing, okay?

286
00:16:09,534 --> 00:16:11,154
Right. Thanks.

287
00:16:15,934 --> 00:16:17,094
There he is, finally.

288
00:16:18,144 --> 00:16:19,264
What do you mean?!

289
00:16:19,944 --> 00:16:24,514
You were just skipping class. I have no desire to
help anyone out who would do such a thing.

290
00:16:24,514 --> 00:16:28,174
What the heck?! If you don't want
to help me out, just say so!

291
00:16:28,354 --> 00:16:30,074
All right. I don't want to. I refuse.

292
00:16:30,884 --> 00:16:32,214
Forget it!

293
00:16:34,154 --> 00:16:36,124
Darn! I should never have asked
that jerk in the first place!

294
00:16:40,664 --> 00:16:42,134
What are you doing here?

295
00:16:43,064 --> 00:16:44,864
Fujimoto, you're mean!

296
00:16:44,864 --> 00:16:45,954
Why do you say that?

297
00:16:46,134 --> 00:16:49,334
You didn't have to talk mean to her like that!

298
00:16:49,404 --> 00:16:52,374
You purposely made her mad at you!

299
00:16:52,504 --> 00:16:54,634
Otherwise they'll come back for more.

300
00:16:54,914 --> 00:16:57,514
Those people might have
had a very good reason!

301
00:16:57,514 --> 00:17:01,504
None of my business.
They ought to fend for themselves.

302
00:17:03,884 --> 00:17:06,754
You forgot this! Now it's delivered!

303
00:17:13,224 --> 00:17:14,214
Kobato...

304
00:17:21,904 --> 00:17:25,104
I shouldn't have spoken to him like that.

305
00:17:28,014 --> 00:17:28,874
Kobato.

306
00:17:30,274 --> 00:17:31,674
Domoto...

307
00:17:32,644 --> 00:17:37,214
You were so kind to help me find Fujimoto,
but I ran off without even thanking you.

308
00:17:37,754 --> 00:17:39,724
Um, I'm sorry.

309
00:17:40,024 --> 00:17:41,614
Relax. Have a seat.

310
00:17:45,964 --> 00:17:48,954
Kobato, how long have you known Fujimoto?

311
00:17:50,064 --> 00:17:53,264
Um, since this spring.

312
00:17:53,604 --> 00:17:54,834
I see.

313
00:17:55,274 --> 00:17:56,564
Why do you ask?

314
00:17:57,374 --> 00:17:59,504
I guess I just felt envious.

315
00:17:59,504 --> 00:18:00,544
Huh?

316
00:18:00,544 --> 00:18:02,534
You know. You and Fujimoto.

317
00:18:02,714 --> 00:18:05,834
Me... and Fujimoto?

318
00:18:06,844 --> 00:18:13,584
I've known him longer than you have,
but I can't talk to him like you do.

319
00:18:14,054 --> 00:18:18,284
Yes, I'm sure Fujimoto
feels terrible after that.

320
00:18:18,624 --> 00:18:21,184
I was really rude to him.

321
00:18:21,264 --> 00:18:23,354
No, that's not what I mean.

322
00:18:24,164 --> 00:18:26,154
What you said was correct.

323
00:18:26,934 --> 00:18:30,564
But I can't even tell him what I think is right.

324
00:18:32,544 --> 00:18:35,204
Sorry, I'm just wishing for
what I don't have, I guess.

325
00:18:35,374 --> 00:18:39,504
You have a lot of wonderful features.

326
00:18:39,614 --> 00:18:41,414
You're very kind, for one...

327
00:18:41,884 --> 00:18:43,784
I'm not at all kind.

328
00:18:43,784 --> 00:18:49,484
What? But people come and ask you for your
help. And you help them out. You're very kind.

329
00:18:50,024 --> 00:18:51,214
Well that...

330
00:18:51,394 --> 00:18:53,654
It's simply because I have trouble saying "no".

331
00:18:53,964 --> 00:18:59,454
If I'm really thinking for the good of that person,
I should be refusing, like Fujimoto does.

332
00:19:01,804 --> 00:19:06,674
You were just skipping class. I have no desire to
help anyone out who would do such a thing.

333
00:19:07,544 --> 00:19:13,104
Fujimoto isn't afraid of making
enemies. He's strong.

334
00:19:13,914 --> 00:19:18,354
People probably avoid him because
they're intimidated by that strength.

335
00:19:19,624 --> 00:19:22,854
I envy him... for that strength of his.

336
00:19:24,124 --> 00:19:26,754
Envy him for his strength?

337
00:19:28,894 --> 00:19:30,154
Yeah.

338
00:19:34,904 --> 00:19:41,364
I don't know about Fujimoto, but having
people afraid of you is a lonely thing.

339
00:19:42,314 --> 00:19:44,474
Being disliked is painful.

340
00:19:46,414 --> 00:19:51,974
All those people I met today. The moment they
found out that you'd help, they looked so happy.

341
00:19:52,454 --> 00:19:53,624
But that's...

342
00:19:53,624 --> 00:19:54,784
Domoto.

343
00:19:55,794 --> 00:19:59,554
Is not wanting to be disliked a bad thing?

344
00:19:59,994 --> 00:20:03,364
Is it bad to want to be liked?

345
00:20:04,134 --> 00:20:07,154
Is it bad to try to help people?

346
00:20:07,874 --> 00:20:12,064
Is wanting to do something for someone
who is in trouble a bad thing?

347
00:20:14,374 --> 00:20:19,334
I don't know how to say this well,
but you are a good person.

348
00:20:26,684 --> 00:20:27,784
Thank you.

349
00:20:30,494 --> 00:20:32,284
You're an unusual girl.

350
00:20:33,464 --> 00:20:36,654
Huh? D-Did I say something strange?

351
00:20:37,064 --> 00:20:41,054
Ioryogi-san always gets upset with me,
saying I don't know anything!

352
00:20:41,574 --> 00:20:42,764
Ioryogi-san?

353
00:20:43,434 --> 00:20:46,994
Yes! Ioryogi-san is a stuffed
toy animal, but he talks!

354
00:20:47,274 --> 00:20:49,944
He talks, but I'm not to speak to him!

355
00:20:49,944 --> 00:20:51,034
Hey!

356
00:20:51,344 --> 00:20:53,314
Is Ioryogi-san that doll?

357
00:20:53,314 --> 00:20:54,244
Yes!

358
00:20:54,244 --> 00:20:55,514
Domoto!

359
00:20:55,914 --> 00:20:57,474
Oh. The girls from earlier.

360
00:20:58,424 --> 00:20:59,644
I'd better go, then.

361
00:20:59,854 --> 00:21:02,054
Yes! Thank you very much!

362
00:21:02,724 --> 00:21:05,154
No, thank you. See you.

363
00:21:05,494 --> 00:21:06,624
Yes!

364
00:21:08,934 --> 00:21:10,294
What?!

365
00:21:10,294 --> 00:21:12,264
Why is there another kompeito?!

366
00:21:13,334 --> 00:21:17,894
Because you acknowledged the
kindness of that good-looking guy.

367
00:21:18,244 --> 00:21:21,734
The good-looking guy?
Are you talking about Domoto?

368
00:21:21,814 --> 00:21:23,214
Who else?!

369
00:21:23,214 --> 00:21:26,614
But, but, does just
acknowledging deserve a kompeito?

370
00:21:26,814 --> 00:21:30,914
Regardless of what others think,
some people are very self-conscious.

371
00:21:31,324 --> 00:21:33,014
Is that right?

372
00:21:33,484 --> 00:21:37,484
Yeah, just tells you good-looking guys
have good-looking guys' problems.

373
00:21:39,264 --> 00:21:42,714
By the way, Dobato. About this afternoon.

374
00:21:43,194 --> 00:21:44,134
Yes?

375
00:21:44,534 --> 00:21:48,104
What was the big idea telling that guy about me!

376
00:21:48,104 --> 00:21:52,264
But, but! I didn't speak to you, just as you said!

377
00:21:52,544 --> 00:21:55,174
The moment you tell people about stuffed
toys that talk and talking to stuffed toys,

378
00:21:55,174 --> 00:21:56,944
you've already gone overboard!

379
00:21:56,944 --> 00:21:59,284
I'm sorry!

380
00:21:59,284 --> 00:22:00,334
Kobato!

381
00:22:01,014 --> 00:22:02,014
30 points!

382
00:22:02,014 --> 00:22:03,914
What?!

383
00:22:03,984 --> 00:22:06,384
No way!

384
00:22:08,394 --> 00:22:09,554
Huh?

385
00:22:10,254 --> 00:22:12,094
I said you were a big help.

386
00:22:16,434 --> 00:22:19,134
That's the same old Fujimoto.

387
00:22:19,134 --> 00:22:20,604
Huh? Huh?

388
00:22:20,904 --> 00:22:26,064
He's pathetic. That guy. In his own way,
he's thanking you the best he knows how.

389
00:22:26,374 --> 00:22:27,534
Thanking me?

390
00:22:28,314 --> 00:22:32,174
Kobato, Teacher Fujimoto isn't
mad at you anymore, is he?

391
00:22:32,284 --> 00:22:35,884
He isn't scary, either. He's a gentle person.

392
00:22:35,884 --> 00:22:36,714
Huh?

393
00:22:36,714 --> 00:22:41,554
He's gentle and kind. He found my house
key for me once when I lost it!

394
00:22:41,654 --> 00:22:43,624
He made a bamboo dragonfly for me once.

395
00:22:43,624 --> 00:22:46,294
Oh, he once gave me a cicada shell.

396
00:22:46,294 --> 00:22:46,864
That's right, and remember that snake slough?

397
00:22:46,864 --> 00:22:48,354
He's not a bad guy.
That's right, and remember that snake slough?

398
00:22:49,034 --> 00:22:50,324
Right?!

399
00:22:53,434 --> 00:22:56,804
He's an unusual person, Fujimoto.

400
00:23:01,344 --> 00:23:08,974
Everyone dreams of flying

401
00:23:10,154 --> 00:23:16,254
But they let gravity trick them

402
00:23:16,524 --> 00:23:24,364
Honestly, everyone is already able to fly

403
00:23:26,604 --> 00:23:32,934
I bet the reason that child looks so terribly sad

404
00:23:33,974 --> 00:23:36,844
Is because he

405
00:23:36,844 --> 00:23:43,974
Accidentally lost his shadow somewhere

406
00:23:44,154 --> 00:23:46,674
In that case

407
00:23:46,854 --> 00:23:50,954
If I could just tell you, "Thank you,"

408
00:23:50,954 --> 00:23:54,834
And you laugh and reply, "Thank you"

409
00:23:54,834 --> 00:24:02,164
That exchange would fill you with joy

410
00:24:02,704 --> 00:24:06,934
It would make you feel so happy

411
00:24:07,244 --> 00:24:11,484
There's nothing to worry about

412
00:24:11,484 --> 00:24:15,574
Since we're together

413
00:24:17,354 --> 00:24:23,294
It's strange how I'm crying

414
00:24:23,294 --> 00:24:26,094
Even though I'm happy

415
00:24:26,094 --> 00:24:29,034
Next episode
...A Kitten's Lullaby.
Even though I'm happy

416
00:24:29,034 --> 00:24:30,794
Next episode
...A Kitten's Lullaby.

